WEBVTT

00:01.001 --> 00:04.879
♪ <i>It seems today that all you see</i> ♪

00:04.880 --> 00:08.174
♪ <i>Is violence in movies and sex on TV</i> ♪

00:08.175 --> 00:11.886
♪ <i>But where are those</i>
<i>good old-fashioned values</i> ♪

00:11.887 --> 00:14.847
♪ <i>On which we used to rely?</i> ♪

00:14.848 --> 00:18.184
♪ <i>Lucky there's a family guy</i> ♪

00:18.185 --> 00:21.604
♪ <i>Lucky there's a man</i>
<i>who positively can do</i> ♪

00:21.605 --> 00:23.064
♪ <i>All the things that make us</i> ♪

00:23.065 --> 00:24.690
♪ <i>Laugh and cry</i> ♪

00:24.691 --> 00:30.155
♪ <i>He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy!</i> ♪

00:36.912 --> 00:39.538
Thanks for coming
to our cocktail party, everyone.

00:39.539 --> 00:41.666
We're so glad you could make it.

00:41.667 --> 00:43.084
That's the speech you were working on?

00:43.085 --> 00:44.710
Okay, now let's play a game.

00:44.711 --> 00:46.295
It's called: "Everybody give me an idea

00:46.296 --> 00:47.713
what time you're leaving."

00:47.714 --> 00:49.173
Settle down, Peter.

00:49.174 --> 00:51.300
Hey, is the party
good out there? Can I come out?

00:51.301 --> 00:53.261
No, Brian, you're fine in the kitchen.

00:53.262 --> 00:55.683
Is there food on the floor?
I can clean it up!

00:55.684 --> 00:57.056
- No.
- Oh, come on.

00:57.057 --> 00:59.100
Joe just dropped a cracker.
Joe just dropped a cracker!

00:59.101 --> 01:01.560
Damn it, Brian!

01:01.561 --> 01:04.522
I can't figure out how to open the gate.

01:04.523 --> 01:06.607
Well, since this is
a nice cocktail party,

01:06.608 --> 01:08.401
let's talk about books.

01:08.402 --> 01:10.364
What book is everyone reading?

01:10.365 --> 01:12.071
I only read four books in my life,

01:12.072 --> 01:14.323
and three of them were
about Johnny Bench.

01:14.324 --> 01:15.574
Ah, I can top that.

01:15.575 --> 01:17.493
I ain't ever read a book
in my entire life.

01:19.121 --> 01:20.746
- Never read a book?
- Peter's never read a book!

01:20.747 --> 01:22.707
Yeah, I heard the first guy.

01:22.708 --> 01:25.960
And you said
this was a fancy cocktail party.

01:25.961 --> 01:27.878
Reginald, we're leaving!

01:30.716 --> 01:32.633
Damn it! I shopped at Trader Joe's

01:32.634 --> 01:35.136
for this fancy cocktail party,
and once again,

01:35.137 --> 01:37.073
your ignorance of books has ruined it.

01:37.074 --> 01:38.431
Enough is enough.

01:38.432 --> 01:41.100
I got a junior high book list
here, and starting tomorrow,

01:41.101 --> 01:42.978
you are reading one of these books.

01:42.979 --> 01:46.193
<i>Little Women, Holes, The Giver.</i>

01:46.194 --> 01:48.649
These are all porn categories.
<i>Black Beauty.</i>

01:48.650 --> 01:50.735
Is there anything here
that's not pornography?

01:50.736 --> 01:53.362
<i>1984!</i> Just read<i> 1984.</i>

01:53.363 --> 01:55.781
Fine. Geez. I'll read<i> 1984.</i>

01:55.782 --> 01:57.992
You better, 'cause this was
more embarrassing

01:57.993 --> 02:01.162
than when we played truth or
dare with present-day Madonna.

02:01.163 --> 02:03.873
Ah... truth.

02:03.874 --> 02:06.125
Do I look younger than 90?

02:06.126 --> 02:07.669
Dare.

02:11.920 --> 02:14.258
Ah, the public library.

02:14.259 --> 02:16.886
I'm just gonna put my backpack
down for one second.

02:16.887 --> 02:18.137
And it's gone.

02:18.138 --> 02:19.722
My laptop was in there, no password.

02:19.723 --> 02:20.973
My wallet. Everything.

02:20.974 --> 02:22.391
That person is now me.

02:22.392 --> 02:24.268
My entire life went away.

02:24.269 --> 02:26.604
Hey, how do you find something in here?

02:26.605 --> 02:29.732
It's a lot easier
than finding a man out there.

02:32.368 --> 02:34.153
Yeah. Yeah, maybe wash your hair,

02:34.154 --> 02:35.905
lose the bun, give that a chance.

02:35.906 --> 02:37.656
Anyway, you guys have<i> 1984?</i>

02:37.657 --> 02:39.700
We've got it on CD.

02:39.701 --> 02:41.410
"C-D."

02:41.411 --> 02:44.830
Sounds like my high school report card.

02:44.831 --> 02:47.667
Okay, okay, all right, all right.

02:49.878 --> 02:52.254
Okay, boring book:<i> 1984.</i>

02:52.255 --> 02:54.006
I am ready for you to be lame

02:54.007 --> 02:56.217
and a book and not something unexpected.

03:00.555 --> 03:03.057
- ♪<i> Oh, yeah...</i> ♪
- This is books?

03:03.058 --> 03:07.354
- Books kick ass!
- ♪<i> Panama, Pana...</i> ♪

03:09.272 --> 03:11.858
Probably reading Orwell.

03:14.986 --> 03:17.222
Kids, where's your father?

03:17.223 --> 03:18.506
He left a note.

03:18.507 --> 03:20.741
"If Van Halen calls,
tell them they rule."

03:20.742 --> 03:22.034
What?

03:22.035 --> 03:24.870
♪ <i>Panama...</i> ♪

03:24.871 --> 03:27.957
- Did they call?
- Peter, what are you doing?!

03:27.958 --> 03:31.530
I did what you wanted. I went
to the library and I got<i> 1984.</i>

03:31.531 --> 03:34.046
What a book!

03:34.047 --> 03:37.216
Peter, I'm not okay with this
new Van Halen phase of yours.

03:37.217 --> 03:39.093
Yeah, Dad, it's crazy.

03:39.094 --> 03:43.180
Like JFK deciding to cruise
through Dallas in a rental.

03:43.181 --> 03:44.890
How'd that convertible work out for you?

03:44.891 --> 03:47.560
Yeah, I don't... I don't know.
Good. Okay.

03:47.561 --> 03:49.937
And did you get all your stuff
out of the car?

03:49.938 --> 03:52.189
Kind of.

03:52.190 --> 03:53.607
♪ <i>Panama...</i> ♪

03:53.608 --> 03:55.234
<i>All units, this is Dispatch.</i>

03:55.235 --> 03:57.820
<i>We've got a red station wagon
blasting "Panama"</i>

03:57.821 --> 03:59.989
<i>and being awesome
and partying and being rad.</i>

03:59.990 --> 04:02.450
Not in my town, Dispatch.

04:02.451 --> 04:06.162
This is Officer Stickbutt, in pursuit.

04:06.163 --> 04:07.621
♪ <i>Whoo!</i> ♪

04:10.000 --> 04:12.126
<i>Stickbutt, break off pursuit.</i>

04:12.127 --> 04:14.837
<i>"Panama" kicks too much ass
and shreds way too hard.</i>

04:14.838 --> 04:16.422
<i>You'll never catch him.</i>

04:16.423 --> 04:18.424
Negative, Dispatch. Just need to wait

04:18.425 --> 04:21.510
for that "Runnin' a little bit
hot tonight" part.

04:21.511 --> 04:23.846
♪ <i>Yeah, we're runnin'</i>
<i>a little bit hot tonight</i> ♪

04:23.847 --> 04:27.349
Bingo. Got him now.

04:27.350 --> 04:29.143
♪ <i>I can barely see the road</i> ♪

04:29.144 --> 04:30.436
♪ <i>From the heat coming off of it</i> ♪

04:32.355 --> 04:33.939
What's he doing?!

04:33.940 --> 04:37.109
Suspect is headed
toward Unjumpable Canyon.

04:37.110 --> 04:39.403
- It's totally unjumpable!
- ♪<i> Ease the seat back...</i> ♪

04:39.404 --> 04:42.948
- Unless...
<i>- Unless what, Stickbutt? Over.</i>

04:42.949 --> 04:45.451
Dear God, he's gonna do it.

04:45.452 --> 04:48.621
He's gonna time his jump for the
greatest harmonized sound drop

04:48.622 --> 04:50.539
in '80s rock history.

04:50.540 --> 04:52.291
<i>You're right. The part that goes...</i>

04:52.292 --> 04:54.126
♪ <i>Ain't no stoppin'</i> ♪

04:54.127 --> 04:58.380
♪ <i>Now...!</i> ♪

05:04.137 --> 05:06.055
- ♪<i> Panama</i> ♪
- Damn it!

05:06.056 --> 05:08.307
<i>- What? What happened?</i>
- Get off this channel, Joe.

05:08.308 --> 05:10.893
<i>Come on, I want to be an outside cop!</i>

05:10.894 --> 05:12.812
♪ <i>Panama.</i> ♪

05:18.026 --> 05:20.819
♪ <i>Panama.</i> ♪

05:20.820 --> 05:22.738
Damn it, Peter, I'm sick of this!

05:22.739 --> 05:25.074
Take that Van Halen CD back today.

05:25.075 --> 05:26.825
No way. I ain't never returning that CD.

05:26.826 --> 05:28.994
It's too awesome.

05:28.995 --> 05:30.871
I didn't want to play this card,
Peter, but

05:30.872 --> 05:32.498
if you won't listen to me,

05:32.499 --> 05:35.209
listen to the pancake
with slices of banana on it.

05:35.210 --> 05:37.002
Oh, my God.

05:37.003 --> 05:38.837
But you're always smiling.

05:38.838 --> 05:40.673
Note the maple syrup tears.

05:40.674 --> 05:43.677
Don't you think I see
the maple syrup tears, Lois?!

05:47.764 --> 05:50.642
I guess my Van Halen days are over.

05:56.022 --> 05:58.566
No, no, no. Those days are behind me.

05:58.567 --> 06:00.694
I made a promise to a pancake.

06:02.737 --> 06:04.697
♪ <i>On and on</i> ♪

06:04.698 --> 06:08.075
♪ <i>He just keeps on trying</i> ♪

06:08.076 --> 06:12.246
♪ <i>And he smiles</i>
<i>when he feels like crying...</i> ♪

06:12.247 --> 06:14.748
♪ <i>Panama</i> ♪

06:14.749 --> 06:16.417
- ♪<i> On and on</i> ♪
- ♪<i> Panama</i> ♪

06:16.418 --> 06:18.419
♪ <i>On and on</i> ♪

06:18.420 --> 06:20.421
♪<i> Pan...</i> ♪

06:20.422 --> 06:23.424
♪ <i>Ain't nothin' like it,</i>
<i>her shiny machine</i> ♪

06:23.425 --> 06:27.094
♪ <i>Got the feel for the wheel,</i>
<i>keep the movin' parts clean</i> ♪

06:27.095 --> 06:28.846
♪ <i>Hot shoe</i> ♪

06:28.847 --> 06:31.223
- Yeah!
- ♪<i> Burnin' down the avenue</i> ♪

06:31.224 --> 06:33.601
- ♪<i> Got an on...</i> ♪
- ♪<i> On and on...</i> ♪

06:33.602 --> 06:38.105
♪ <i>Bedroom, don't you know</i>
<i>she's coming home with me?</i> ♪

06:38.106 --> 06:40.524
- ♪<i> You'll lose her in the turn</i> ♪
- Working squirrel.

06:51.119 --> 06:52.911
Hey, in case you need it,

06:52.912 --> 06:55.080
someone left this business card
at the crash site.

06:55.081 --> 06:57.916
Looks like there's a new
squirrel in the insurance game.

06:57.917 --> 06:59.752
I don't care about that, Dr. Hartman.

06:59.753 --> 07:02.504
Just tell me
what's wrong with my husband.

07:02.505 --> 07:04.923
I'm sorry, Mrs. Griffin,
but your husband

07:04.924 --> 07:06.800
is in a coma.

07:06.801 --> 07:08.469
Oh, my God!

07:08.470 --> 07:10.929
And to deliver the news
to your teenage children,

07:10.930 --> 07:12.806
I've hired an EDM DJ.

07:12.807 --> 07:14.767
♪ <i>Your father's in a coma</i> ♪

07:14.768 --> 07:17.019
♪ <i>Coma, coma, coma, coma, coma</i> ♪

07:17.020 --> 07:18.771
♪<i> He's gonna die.</i> ♪

07:18.772 --> 07:20.689
This is awesome!

07:20.690 --> 07:24.027
Yeah, I saw this guy playing
at an H&M, and I got his number!

07:30.909 --> 07:33.519
My husband is in a coma?!

07:33.520 --> 07:34.920
I'm afraid so.

07:34.921 --> 07:36.830
I mean, he's not responding
to my advances,

07:36.831 --> 07:39.333
so it's either a coma,
or he's a frigid bitch.

07:39.334 --> 07:40.834
We'll leave you with him now.

07:40.835 --> 07:42.836
But it's very important
that you speak to Peter.

07:42.837 --> 07:44.463
He can hear you.

07:44.464 --> 07:46.965
Talk about the good times,
what he means to you.

07:46.966 --> 07:49.010
Talk and keep talking.

07:57.977 --> 08:00.939
Psh-psh-pshew.

08:01.898 --> 08:04.566
Let's just turn on the TV.

08:04.567 --> 08:06.611
We now return to</i> The Simpsons.

08:10.699 --> 08:12.408
Meme.

08:12.409 --> 08:13.992
Not a meme.

08:13.993 --> 08:15.994
Meme.

08:15.995 --> 08:17.080
Not a meme.

08:18.791 --> 08:21.578
Where am I? Hey, let me out. Let me out!

08:23.837 --> 08:28.216
Hello, Peter.

09:08.715 --> 09:11.842
What did I ever do to deserve this?!

09:11.843 --> 09:15.012
Oh, no! Oh, no! Oh, no!

09:15.013 --> 09:16.513
Oh, yeah!

09:18.767 --> 09:20.851
<i>The Godfather</i> insists upon itself.

09:20.852 --> 09:23.228
- It insists upon itself.
- It insists upon itself.

09:23.229 --> 09:25.272
<i>The Godfather</i> insists upon itself.

09:25.273 --> 09:27.357
- It insists upon itself.
- It insists upon itself.

09:27.358 --> 09:29.026
It insists upon itself.

09:29.027 --> 09:30.611
<i>The Godfather</i> insists upon itself.

09:30.612 --> 09:31.945
- It insists...
- It insists...

09:31.946 --> 09:34.031
Ah, no! Wait! I agree with all of you!

09:34.032 --> 09:35.158
Upon itself.

09:41.080 --> 09:43.415
Has the jury reached a verdict?

09:43.416 --> 09:44.917
We have, Your Honor.

09:44.918 --> 09:46.919
And how do you find the defendant?

09:46.920 --> 09:49.296
B'caw, or not b'caw?

09:49.297 --> 09:52.633
We find the defendant,
Peter Griffin, b'caw.

09:55.929 --> 09:59.139
Peter Griffin, I hereby sentence you

09:59.140 --> 10:02.976
to an awkward apology dinner
with Joaquin Phoenix.

10:06.981 --> 10:10.067
Well... I'm waiting.

10:10.068 --> 10:12.694
Hey, if, uh, this goes south,

10:12.695 --> 10:16.281
is there a plan for Peter's rakes?

10:16.282 --> 10:18.784
Um... who's gonna get Peter's rakes?

10:18.785 --> 10:21.161
What did I tell you, Mom?
What did I tell you?

10:21.162 --> 10:22.621
Well, I just thought
it would be one less thing

10:22.622 --> 10:24.039
to worry about later.

10:24.040 --> 10:26.542
You came out
of the blocks too soon, Joe.

10:26.543 --> 10:29.545
Oh, Lois, I came as soon as I heard.

10:29.546 --> 10:33.298
So... h-have you guys made
any arrangements rake-wise?

10:33.299 --> 10:35.676
Bonnie. Ix-nay on the akes-ray.

10:39.889 --> 10:41.306
Clear!

10:41.307 --> 10:44.601
No, you do stuff up here. Clear!

10:44.602 --> 10:46.019
Clear!

10:46.020 --> 10:48.522
Clear!

10:48.523 --> 10:49.898
Clear!

10:49.899 --> 10:52.025
Clear!

10:54.028 --> 10:56.989
No, that's the good sound.

10:56.990 --> 10:59.283
Oh, well, why don't you
just do everything.

10:59.284 --> 11:01.201
I hate this stupid hospital.

11:01.202 --> 11:03.161
Clear!

11:09.711 --> 11:11.886
- What are they all doing here?
- The canal.

11:11.887 --> 11:13.755
- She is finished.
- What canal?

11:13.756 --> 11:16.842
Think, senor.
What is your new favorite song?

11:16.843 --> 11:18.510
- "Panama"?
<i>- Sí.</i>

11:18.511 --> 11:19.928
It is the Panama Canal.

11:19.929 --> 11:21.930
Your President Woodrow Wilson

11:21.931 --> 11:24.516
is giving the dedication right now.

11:24.517 --> 11:27.686
Ah, you reach down between my legs.

11:27.687 --> 11:29.688
Ease the seat back.

11:29.689 --> 11:32.685
Got the feeling. Power steering.

11:32.686 --> 11:34.282
Pistons popping.

11:34.283 --> 11:36.862
Ain't no stopping now, Panama.

11:39.032 --> 11:41.033
And now, senor, you must pee.

11:41.034 --> 11:43.243
- What?
- Pee. You must pee.

11:43.244 --> 11:44.996
Fill the canal.

11:47.040 --> 11:49.291
Well, it's gonna take a minute.

11:49.292 --> 11:51.793
- You see<i> Coco?</i>
- Of course.

11:51.794 --> 11:54.713
- It's good, right?
- It's very good.

11:54.714 --> 11:57.382
Okay, I'm gonna try pulling
my pants all the way down.

11:57.383 --> 11:59.801
Sometimes that helps.

11:59.802 --> 12:02.394
- It wasn't a true story, right?
- What?

12:02.395 --> 12:04.056
<i>- Coco.</i>
- No, it was fiction.

12:04.057 --> 12:06.635
Somebody make it up out of their head.

12:06.636 --> 12:08.060
Aw, that's too bad.

12:08.061 --> 12:10.896
I can't go. Can't we
just fill this up with a hose?

12:10.897 --> 12:13.107
Oh, yeah. Turn on the hose!

12:19.948 --> 12:21.114
Mayor West?

12:21.115 --> 12:22.762
Angela?

12:22.763 --> 12:24.076
My dad?

12:24.077 --> 12:27.358
Quagmire's fat girlfriend
who died in the<i> Clue</i> episode?

12:27.359 --> 12:29.081
What do all these people have in common?

12:29.082 --> 12:32.126
And how do they know
I like being slowly beckoned?

12:37.423 --> 12:40.467
Mrs. Griffin, I have
some good news or some bad news

12:40.468 --> 12:42.796
depending on how you feel
about your husband.

12:42.797 --> 12:44.638
- Do you love your husband?
- Yes.

12:44.639 --> 12:46.431
Mrs. Griffin, I have some bad news.

12:46.432 --> 12:48.642
Your husband is brain-dead.

12:48.643 --> 12:52.062
I'm afraid it's time
for you to... make your choice.

12:52.063 --> 12:55.482
What? A-Are you telling me
I should pull the plug?

12:55.483 --> 12:56.900
I'm afraid so.

12:56.901 --> 12:58.527
Also, you might be getting a call

12:58.528 --> 13:00.278
about the service
you received here today.

13:00.279 --> 13:02.280
Do you feel I've earned all tens?

13:02.281 --> 13:04.616
Oh, God, I-I don't know.

13:04.617 --> 13:06.284
I can't get anything less than a ten,

13:06.285 --> 13:07.494
so if there's a problem,

13:07.495 --> 13:08.787
you should tell me about it right now.

13:08.788 --> 13:10.789
I may have to pull the plug
on my husband.

13:10.790 --> 13:12.457
Yeah, I-I can't do anything about that.

13:12.458 --> 13:16.003
But really, we-we really,
really, really need the tens.

13:16.004 --> 13:18.547
I-It's two minutes for you.
It's a job or not for me.

13:20.133 --> 13:22.175
Hello?

13:22.176 --> 13:23.677
Six.

13:23.678 --> 13:25.637
Yeah, six across the board.

13:25.638 --> 13:27.223
Ah, nuts.

13:29.475 --> 13:32.853
Senor Griffin, I think it's time
for you to depart.

13:32.854 --> 13:35.939
Thanks, Jose, probably.
Thanks for everything.

13:35.940 --> 13:38.483
Hey, before I go, what's
the boat's Wi-Fi password?

13:38.484 --> 13:40.694
Oh, there's no Wi-Fi on board.

13:40.695 --> 13:42.946
I don't want to go!

13:42.947 --> 13:45.450
I don't want to go!

13:47.368 --> 13:49.619
- Hey.
- Hey.

13:49.620 --> 13:52.539
That's a... that's a plug.

13:52.540 --> 13:55.834
You... You pulled the plug on me?

13:55.835 --> 13:58.507
Peter, it was a very difficult decision.

13:58.508 --> 14:00.464
How could you do that? I'm alive.

14:00.465 --> 14:02.007
I'm here from the mortgage company.

14:02.008 --> 14:04.843
Mr. Griffin, you're three months
late on your payment.

14:07.013 --> 14:08.555
Oh, he died.

14:08.556 --> 14:09.931
Oh, that's too bad.

14:09.932 --> 14:12.517
Mind if I turn on
my cotton candy machine?

14:14.729 --> 14:17.440
Aw, you got me.

14:23.821 --> 14:25.864
Hey, sweetheart. How you feeling?

14:25.865 --> 14:28.784
Terrible! My family tried
to off me in my sleep.

14:28.785 --> 14:30.744
We said we're sorry, all right?

14:30.745 --> 14:32.537
We're sorry we pulled the plug!

14:32.538 --> 14:35.373
- But you know what? It was a relief.
- What?

14:35.374 --> 14:38.043
There! I said it. You know what
it's like being married to you?

14:38.044 --> 14:39.711
Every day wondering

14:39.712 --> 14:42.130
if my husband's gonna die
from something stupid?

14:42.131 --> 14:44.591
Crashing your Petercopter.
Getting eaten at the zoo.

14:44.592 --> 14:46.968
Running into a tunnel
that's not really a tunnel

14:46.969 --> 14:48.386
but just something
the Road Runner painted

14:48.387 --> 14:49.846
on the side of a rock.

14:49.847 --> 14:51.223
Yeah, well, I saw<i> him</i> go through it.

14:51.224 --> 14:53.558
Honestly, I-I'm amazed you haven't died

14:53.559 --> 14:56.770
in some kind of<i> Black Mirror</i>
techno nightmare by now.

14:56.771 --> 14:58.146
Excuse me.

14:58.147 --> 14:59.940
I have to take this phone call from...

14:59.941 --> 15:03.361
Me?!

15:09.242 --> 15:12.410
This me took a picture of dog poo.

15:12.411 --> 15:14.579
The thought of losing you
was such a burden.

15:14.580 --> 15:17.582
So when the moment came, I confess.

15:17.583 --> 15:19.751
I-I felt free, and I did it.

15:19.752 --> 15:20.836
I pulled the plug.

15:20.837 --> 15:23.255
And then I instantly regretted it.

15:23.256 --> 15:25.173
And when you woke up, I was overjoyed.

15:25.174 --> 15:27.926
I'm so sorry, and if there's any way

15:27.927 --> 15:30.929
I can make it up to you,
I will. I promise.

15:30.930 --> 15:32.264
We all will.

15:32.265 --> 15:33.932
Damn right
you're gonna make it up to me.

15:33.933 --> 15:35.517
I am gonna be more high-maintenance

15:35.518 --> 15:37.727
than a white woman on vacation.

15:37.728 --> 15:40.188
Excuse me, could I get
<i>dos</i> margaritas, por favor?

15:40.189 --> 15:43.294
Yoo-hoo! Hello? Senor?

15:43.295 --> 15:46.230
Excuse me? Could I get towels?
We need more towels.

15:46.231 --> 15:48.655
Wh-When you get a chance, but right now.

15:48.656 --> 15:52.535
Is someone available
to take 20 to 40 pictures of me?

15:56.539 --> 15:57.956
Family, you know how
you said you're sorry

15:57.957 --> 16:00.125
- and you'll do anything I want?
- Yeah.

16:00.126 --> 16:01.668
Well, this is Timothy Olyphant.

16:01.669 --> 16:04.337
I want you to line up
and give him one compliment

16:04.338 --> 16:06.715
about his Netflix show,
the<i> Santa Clarita Diet.</i>

16:06.716 --> 16:08.967
- Aw, really?
- And it has to sound legit.

16:08.968 --> 16:10.302
Like you've actually watched it.

16:10.303 --> 16:13.013
Peter, you ask too much.

16:13.014 --> 16:15.807
Hey, you tried to kill me.
This is the logical consequence.

16:15.808 --> 16:17.976
Uh, Mr. Olyphant,

16:17.977 --> 16:19.978
I think you were awesome in<i> Deadwood.</i>

16:19.979 --> 16:21.646
No, no, that's not what I said.

16:21.647 --> 16:23.815
The comments have to exclusively relate

16:23.816 --> 16:25.483
to the<i> Santa Clarita Diet,</i>

16:25.484 --> 16:28.653
a show which aired
three full seasons on Netflix.

16:28.654 --> 16:30.989
I will take the first compliment
off the table.

16:30.990 --> 16:32.690
I like your hair.

16:32.691 --> 16:34.232
Well, now I have nothing.

16:34.233 --> 16:36.203
- Come on, kids, we're leaving.
- What?

16:36.204 --> 16:38.079
It's over. You'll never forgive us

16:38.080 --> 16:40.498
for killing you at the hospital,
so we're done.

16:40.499 --> 16:42.375
We're leaving town today.

16:42.376 --> 16:44.129
You... You're leaving?

16:44.130 --> 16:45.670
You'll never hear from us again.

16:45.671 --> 16:47.380
It'll be like<i> we</i> died.

16:47.381 --> 16:49.174
Come on, kids.

16:49.175 --> 16:51.343
No, don't take the kids.

16:51.344 --> 16:55.013
Please. No.
Whatever will I do without them?

16:55.014 --> 16:57.531
Banana pancake, you, too?

16:57.532 --> 16:58.821
You're leaving forever?

16:58.822 --> 17:01.394
I'm actually going to Hedo for Pancakes.

17:01.395 --> 17:03.855
Oh, yeah! The ripping and the tearing.

17:03.856 --> 17:05.190
The ripping and the tearing.

17:05.191 --> 17:07.025
The syrup and the bacon.

17:07.026 --> 17:09.070
The syrup and the...

17:14.867 --> 17:16.368
Well, they're gone.

17:16.369 --> 17:18.370
It's all right. I'll be okay.

17:18.371 --> 17:20.622
And I definitely won't have
any flashbacks

17:20.623 --> 17:23.833
of our happy times together
to convince me otherwise.

17:25.419 --> 17:27.212
♪ <i>Painting the walls</i> ♪

17:27.213 --> 17:29.756
♪ <i>Means happy times</i> ♪

17:29.757 --> 17:32.008
Aw, we were so happy.

17:32.009 --> 17:35.095
♪ <i>And now we're fighting with paint</i> ♪

17:35.096 --> 17:38.265
♪ <i>To show we're having fun</i> ♪

17:38.266 --> 17:40.350
God, I miss those paint fights.

17:40.351 --> 17:43.103
♪ <i>But then the music slows down</i> ♪

17:43.104 --> 17:45.438
♪ <i>'Cause the shuttle blew up</i> ♪

17:45.439 --> 17:49.359
♪ <i>And it really hit home</i> ♪

17:49.360 --> 17:51.778
I don't know why we painted that day.

17:51.779 --> 17:53.071
♪ <i>But then we picked up the pieces</i> ♪

17:53.072 --> 17:56.283
♪ <i>And started painting again</i> ♪

17:56.284 --> 17:57.575
Yay! We overcame!

17:57.576 --> 17:59.786
I got to get my family back.

17:59.787 --> 18:02.747
♪ <i>And who am I? I'm a fly on the wall</i> ♪

18:02.748 --> 18:06.126
♪ <i>A fly who's seen it all.</i> ♪

18:06.127 --> 18:08.754
Ah, damn it. Now we got to repaint.

18:13.009 --> 18:14.759
Come on! I got to get to the airport.

18:14.760 --> 18:17.595
Sorry, bub.
You'll be driving there slow.

18:17.596 --> 18:20.015
Unless you got
some kind of up-tempo rock music

18:20.016 --> 18:21.475
that's good for speeding to.

18:28.607 --> 18:31.032
Mom? What is it?

18:31.033 --> 18:34.279
I-I thought maybe your father
would show up at the last second

18:34.280 --> 18:36.114
and we'd have
one of those airport scenes.

18:36.115 --> 18:39.993
Well, that's a nice movie trope,
Lois, but the post-9/11 reality

18:39.994 --> 18:42.120
is there's no way
a nonticketed civilian can...

18:42.121 --> 18:43.788
♪ <i>Panama...</i> ♪

18:43.789 --> 18:45.123
Lois! Kids!

18:45.124 --> 18:46.624
Dad came.

18:46.625 --> 18:48.209
Brian was wrong again.

18:48.210 --> 18:50.295
He's basically always wrong.

18:50.296 --> 18:52.297
- Peter?
- Guys, please don't go.

18:52.298 --> 18:53.715
I love you.

18:53.716 --> 18:56.009
Oh, Peter,
what made you change your mind?

18:56.010 --> 18:57.802
I just... I've been thinking.

18:57.803 --> 18:59.554
Okay, so you tried to kill me.

18:59.555 --> 19:02.307
But maybe that's what
a family is, you know?

19:02.308 --> 19:04.893
A bunch of people
who try to kill each other.

19:04.894 --> 19:06.853
I don't think that's what a family is.

19:06.854 --> 19:08.188
Eh, it is, kind of.

19:08.189 --> 19:11.066
Anyway, you're my family,
and I love you.

19:11.067 --> 19:14.258
And if I got to have my plug
pulled by somebody,

19:14.259 --> 19:15.959
I want it to be you.

19:15.960 --> 19:18.823
And you're the only people
whose plug I want to pull.

19:18.824 --> 19:20.825
Will you come back?

19:20.826 --> 19:23.499
Yes, Peter. Yes!

19:32.213 --> 19:34.048
All right, everybody switch.

19:36.008 --> 19:37.926
<i>I got a guy.</i>

19:37.927 --> 19:40.054
<i>But I made the rules, so I went with it.</i>

19:45.930 --> 19:48.561
Well, we all learned
an important lesson:

19:48.562 --> 19:50.939
no one should ever read a book.

19:50.940 --> 19:52.607
Eh, I didn't need a coma to know that.

19:54.026 --> 19:55.193
Oh, my God, you guys.

19:55.194 --> 19:58.405
Another space shuttle exploded.

19:58.406 --> 20:01.367
Well, there's only one thing to do.

20:01.368 --> 20:03.289
Let's paint.

20:04.578 --> 20:07.080
♪ <i>Painting the walls</i> ♪

20:07.081 --> 20:11.042
♪ <i>To get through tough times</i> ♪

20:11.043 --> 20:12.919
♪ <i>When shuttles blow up</i> ♪

20:12.920 --> 20:15.463
♪ <i>It's not always an accident</i> ♪

20:15.464 --> 20:17.132
What do you mean, not an accident?

20:17.133 --> 20:19.050
Who is this guy singing?

20:19.051 --> 20:22.095
♪ <i>And who am I? A conspiracy fly</i> ♪

20:22.096 --> 20:26.808
♪ <i>Did you know "NASA"</i>
<i>means "deceive" in Hebrew?</i> ♪

20:26.809 --> 20:27.976
I did not.

20:27.977 --> 20:30.061
♪ <i>The Denver Airport was built</i> ♪

20:30.062 --> 20:34.816
♪ <i>By the Illuminati</i> ♪

20:34.817 --> 20:36.818
Peter, shoo that fly out of here.

20:36.819 --> 20:38.820
I will as soon as I find out if he has

20:38.821 --> 20:41.823
a banned-from-the-Apple-Store
podcast I can listen to.

20:41.824 --> 20:43.324
♪ <i>I do</i> ♪

20:43.325 --> 20:46.911
♪ <i>It's FlyOnTheWall. buzz/truth</i> ♪

20:46.912 --> 20:50.582
♪ <i>First reconfigure your DNS server</i> ♪

20:50.583 --> 20:53.251
♪ <i>Then download a VPN</i> ♪

20:53.252 --> 20:58.756
♪ <i>And get the Tor browser.</i> ♪

20:58.757 --> 21:00.968
It's too much work.